<title>NETHERLANDS: AEA freight tonne-km figures for 96/95 by airline.</title>
<headline>AEA freight tonne-km figures for 96/95 by airline.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freight flown by the 26 members of the Association of European Airlines (AEA) as measured in freight tonnes kilometres traffic rose by 4.5 percent to 25,851 million FTMs in 1996, AEA statistics show.</p>
<p>The statistics, including international and domestic flights, show Lufthansa remained the largest European carrier at 6,019 million FTKs carried on scheduled services</p>
<p>    Ranking		1996	 1995	 percent change</p>
<p>							    '96 vs '95</p>
<p>1.  Lufthansa	  6018.59     5833.06	  up  3.2</p>
<p>2.  Air France	 4656.40     4419.91	  up  5.4</p>
<p>3.  KLM		  3704.24     3602.57	  up  2.8</p>
<p>4.  BA		   3494.41     3252.28	  up  7.4</p>
<p>5.  Cargolux	   2020.00     1941.00	  up  4.1</p>
<p>6.  Swissair	   1622.60     1508.16	  up  7.6</p>
<p>7.  Alitalia	   1456.58     1467.09	down  0.7</p>
<p>8.  Iberia		731.53	678.49	  up  7.8</p>
<p>9.  SAS		   617.37	452.80	  up 36.3</p>
<p>10 .Sabena		338.64	415.14	down 18.4</p>
